{
    "map": {
        "attribute_tolerances.descr": "The numeric value that determines the range in which attribute values are considered equal. This only applies to numeric field types.",
        "attribute_tolerances.dt.title1": "Field",
        "attribute_tolerances.dt.title2": "Tolerance",
        "attribute_tolerances.title": "Attribute Tolerance",
        "compare_status.title": "Compare Status",
        "compare_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>The comparison type. The default is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">All</span>, which will compare all properties of the features being compared.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ALL\">All</span>—All properties of the feature classes will be compared. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"GEOMETRY_ONLY\">Geometry only</span>—Only the geometries of the feature classes will be compared.</li><li><span title=\"ATTRIBUTES_ONLY\">Attributes only</span>—Only the attributes and their values will be compared.</li><li><span title=\"SCHEMA_ONLY\">Schema only</span>—Only the schema of the feature classes will be compared.</li><li><span title=\"SPATIAL_REFERENCE_ONLY\">Spatial Reference only</span>—Only the spatial references of the two feature classes will be compared.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "compare_type.domain.ALL": "All",
        "compare_type.domain.ATTRIBUTES_ONLY": "Attributes only",
        "compare_type.domain.GEOMETRY_ONLY": "Geometry only",
        "compare_type.domain.SCHEMA_ONLY": "Schema only",
        "compare_type.domain.SPATIAL_REFERENCE_ONLY": "Spatial Reference only",
        "compare_type.title": "Compare Type",
        "continue_compare.descr": "<xdoc><p>Indicates whether to compare all properties after encountering the first mismatch.<ul><li>Unchecked—Stops after encountering the first mismatch. This is the default.</li><li>Checked—Compares other properties after encountering the first mismatch.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "continue_compare.title": "Continue Comparison",
        "description": "Compares two feature classes or layers and returns the comparison results.",
        "ignore_options.descr": "<xdoc><p>These properties will not be compared.</p><ul><li><span title=\"IGNORE_M\">Ignore Ms</span>—Do not compare measure properties.</li><li><span title=\"IGNORE_Z\">Ignore Zs</span>—Do not compare elevation properties.</li><li><span title=\"IGNORE_POINTID\">Ignore PointIDs</span>—Do not compare point ID properties.</li><li><span title=\"IGNORE_EXTENSION_PROPERTIES\">Ignore extension properties</span>—Do not compare extension properties.</li><li><span title=\"IGNORE_SUBTYPES\">Ignore subtypes</span>—Do not compare subtypes.</li><li><span title=\"IGNORE_RELATIONSHIPCLASSES\">Ignore relationship classes</span>—Do not compare relationship classes.</li><li><span title=\"IGNORE_REPRESENTATIONCLASSES\">Ignore representation classes</span>—Do not compare representation classes.</li><li><span title=\"IGNORE_FIELDALIAS\">Ignore field alias</span>—Do not compare field aliases.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_EXTENSION_PROPERTIES": "Ignore extension properties",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_FIELDALIAS": "Ignore field alias",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_M": "Ignore Ms",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_POINTID": "Ignore PointIDs",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_RELATIONSHIPCLASSES": "Ignore relationship classes",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_REPRESENTATIONCLASSES": "Ignore representation classes",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_SUBTYPES": "Ignore subtypes",
        "ignore_options.domain.IGNORE_Z": "Ignore Zs",
        "ignore_options.title": "Ignore Options",
        "in_base_features.descr": "<xdoc><p>The <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Base Features</span> are compared with the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Test Features</span>. <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Base Features</span> refers to data that you have declared valid. This base data has the correct geometry definitions, field definitions, and spatial reference.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_base_features.title": "Input Base Features",
        "in_test_features.descr": "<xdoc><p>The <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Test Features</span> are compared against the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Base Features</span>. <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Test Features</span> refers to data that you have made changes to by editing or compiling new features.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_test_features.title": "Input Test Features",
        "m_tolerance.descr": "The measure tolerance is the minimum distance between measures before they are considered equal.",
        "m_tolerance.title": "M Tolerance",
        "omit_field.descr": "The field or fields that will be omitted during comparison. The field definitions and the tabular values for these fields will be ignored.",
        "omit_field.title": "Omit Fields",
        "out_compare_file.descr": "<xdoc><p>This file will contain all similarities and differences between the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Base Features</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Test Features</span>. This file is a comma-delimited text file that can be viewed and used as a table in ArcGIS.</p><p>This file will contain all similarities and differences between the in_base_features and the in_test_features. This file is a comma-delimited text file that can be viewed and used as a table in ArcGIS.</p></xdoc>",
        "out_compare_file.title": "Output Compare File",
        "sort_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The field or fields used to sort records in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Base Features</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Test Features</span>. The records are sorted in ascending order. Sorting by a common field in both the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Base Features</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Input Test Features</span> ensures that you are comparing the same row from each input dataset.</p></xdoc>",
        "sort_field.dt.title1": "Sort Field",
        "sort_field.title": "Sort Field",
        "title": "Feature Compare",
        "xy_tolerance.descr": "The distance that determines the range in which features are considered equal. To minimize error, the value you choose for the compare tolerance should be as small as possible. By default, the compare tolerance is the XY tolerance of the input base features.",
        "xy_tolerance.title": "XY Tolerance",
        "z_tolerance.descr": "The Z Tolerance is the minimum distance between z coordinates before they are considered equal.",
        "z_tolerance.title": "Z Tolerance"
    }
}
